      "text_raw": "Would a BiCMOS folded\nOTA be even faster?\nThe only good position\nfor bipolar transistors to be\nplugged in, is as cascode\ndevices. Indeed, this is where\nwe need the highest-speed\ndevices. The non-dominant\npole at nodes 1 and 2 are\nlinked to the f of the cas-\nT\ncodes. This is higher than\nthe f of the nMOST f\nT T\nwithin a particular\nBiCMOS technology.\nRemember that this is not\nnecessarily higher than for\nnMOSTs in a more recent standard CMOS technology.\nNever use bipolar devices for the transistors M10 and M11 in the DC current sources. Their\ncollector-substrate capacitances would reduce the non-dominant pole at nodes 1 and 2 too much!",
